        <section id="so-what-is-malicious-software?"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
            <h2>So what is Malicious software?</h2>
              <p>We hear the term malicious software all the time but what exactly is it, what does it do, how do we protect ourselves from it and how can we get rid of it when we have it in our systems?</p>
<p>Malicious software or malware is any software that is designed for the purposes of intentionally causing damage or exploiting any programmable device, computer, service, network, or system.</p>
<p>Malicious software can include Viruses, Ransomware, Spyware,Trojans, Worms, Scareware and Adware. Some of these have already been mentioned in previous units but let's refresh our memories on what they involve.</p>
<p>Select the images below to read</p>

              
              <!-- IF 2 --><ul class="l-icon-grid ">
  
  
    
    <!--  -->
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/cs/cs_u4_s2_p1_reveal1.svg" alt="Ransomware" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Ransomware</h3>
      <p>This is the most profitable and therefore the most popular. It installs itself onto a machine, encrypts the files and demands a ransom for the release, usually in bitcoin.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/cs/cs_u4_s2_p1_reveal2.svg" alt="Spyware" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Spyware</h3>
      <p>Once installed spyware captures and transmits personal information and browsing habits. Users of spyware include criminals, as well as security organisations and other consumers as it can also be used to spy on employees, family members and to test and monitor communications in investigations.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/cs/cs_u4_s2_p1_reveal3.svg" alt="Trojans" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Trojans</h3>
      <p>These pretend to be harmless applications tricking users into downloading them, where they then launch their attack, stealing data, spying or crashing systems.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/cs/cs_u4_s2_p1_reveal4.svg" alt="Worms" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Worms</h3>
      <p>Worms copy themselves from machine to machine exploiting weaknesses in software or operating systems.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/cs/cs_u4_s2_p1_reveal5.svg" alt="Scareware" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Scareware</h3>
      <p>Tricks individuals into thinking they have a virus or their system is infected to purchase and download a fake application.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/cs/cs_u4_s2_p1_reveal6.svg" alt="Adware" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Adware</h3>
      <p>Adware programs push unwanted adverts and pop ups at users. These usually accompany the use of software for free.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
  
</ul>

            
          
