          <toggle-section open="false">
            <h3>Video transcript </h3>
            <p><strong>Abraham:</strong> With the large amount of malware out there it will inevitably penetrate and infect a system especially a vulnerable system. This infection maybe caused by downloading a music file, a video file, or any other software from suspicious sites. Also clicking on a link from a suspicious email sent from an unknown email address or even one pretending to be from a trusted contact. The most common signs that a system has been compromised are when a computer slows down, browsers redirect to other sites, infection warnings, offers of software to buy to fix it and pop-up ads, also, problems shutting down and starting up a system. Any of these may suggest that a system is infected.</p>
<p>So how can you stop this happening? Make sure that your system is protected by legitimate 'anti-malware' purchased from a reputable company even if it is a mobile system and that it is kept up to date, both the operating system and any software installed on it such as your web browser. Keep all devices secure and don't download anything from any dodgy sites or click on any unknown links on unreliable emails. Only purchase from official suppliers.</p>
<p>But if you do find that you have Malicious software infecting your system, can it be removed? It is possible to remove malware, by running a scan using the security software installed on the device or system and taking steps to fix the web browser.</p>
<p>Antimalware works in two different ways.</p>
<p>The first is a more outdated approach which works on creating a hash of all files on the system. This hash is then checked against a list of known malicious hashed malware. This is referred to as signature-based detection.</p>
<p>The problem with this method is that it relies on the fact that the malware has been previously identified and at the pace at which malware is being developed this is becoming harder to do.</p>
<p>In response to this a lot of antimalware solutions now work on a heuristic detection method, which looks more at the behaviours of files or processes in a system to identify what could be potentially malicious behaviour.</p>

          </toggle-section>
        
      
          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
  
